<title>USA: Maine court declines to rule on forest referendum.</title>
<headline>Maine court declines to rule on forest referendum.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine's State Supreme Court has refused to advise Gov. Angus King on what to do about forestry in Maine.</p>
<p>At issue is last autumn's referendum in which voters failed to give a clear majority vote to King's so-called compact for Maine forests.</p>
<p>Some legal experts believe the voters must vote again before the legislature can take further action. Lawmakers will meet later this week to consider how to deal with the problem. One possible solution is for the legislature to ask the high court to re-consider its position.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
